xing unit was changed from 3 to  4 at 60 minutes  and reverted to 3 at 120 minutes  gauge set point for second mixing unit  was also changed from 7 to 8  180 minutes and reverted to 7 at 240  minutes  we can see from these spots that the  setpoint tracking was achieved  with fast and accurate response and no  instagram  plus on this slide showed experimental  results for tracking minimum  residence time separates fast from the  top  show flow rate determined by the minimum  resonance time controller  observance measurements at the internet  and outlet of the column  and estimating minimal resonance time  the set points shown as fact dash lines  during the experiment the nmrs time  resistance time set point was changed  from 240 seconds to 300 seconds 180  minutes  and reverted to 240 seconds at 360  minutes  first we can see from the second part  that the resin time distribution model  with estimated primers  will describe the concentration at the  outlet  also we can see from the bottom part  that the set point tracking was achieved  within single step after the resonance  time distribution estimation  moving on to the next validation  experiment disturbance rejection was  tested for ph control by changing the  buffer concentration of the acid stream  from phosphoric acid to citric acid this  was done with a mole still being  initialized with the acid dissociation  constants of phosphoric acid  so the mole is initially not aware of  the buffer change in the answer stream  plus on this slide showed experimental  results for the disturbance rejection of  ph controller  from the top plus show flow rate  determined by the piece controller  p measurements with set points shown as  black dashed lines  and the estimated primary values of acid  dissociation constants  with true values for citric acids shown  as black dash lines we can see from the  second part that the setpoint tracking  was again achieved  with fast and accurate response and no  instability  even with the introduced disturbance we  can also see from the bottom plot  that the map estimation algorithm  quickly estimated the acid dissociation  constants of citric  acid truly from the pitch measurements  in the first few minutes  for the last validation experiment  disturbance rejection was tested for the  minimum resonance time control  by adding an additional length of tubing  in series with the column  while the system is in normal operation  tube clamps were used to remove this  additional length of tubing in the flow  path  as shown in this process for gathering  this effectively led to suddenly  decreasing the active volume through the  column  and therefore suddenly decreasing the  resonance time in the system  the plots in this slide showed  experimental results for disturbance  rejection of minimal resonance time  controller  which vertical line shows the time and  the length of the cube was decreased  with a tube clamped  we can see from the second part that the  mall correctly predicted the output of  each water injection  even after when the sudden disturbance  was introduced into the system  we can see from the bottom part that the  minimum resonance time measurement  correctly identifies the following  change in the system recent time  then the controller adjusts the pump  speed accordingly  and restore the original residence time  set point again in a single step  to conclude in this work we constructed  a low-cost  column-based continuous product equation  system with off-the-shelf components  and controller validation experiments  demonstrated  that ph and minimum residence time  segwaying tracking  and also disturbance rejection are  achieved with fast and accurate response  and no instability  overall this work provided tools for the  design and operation of continuous file  activation systems  in service of increasing productivity  improving product quality  enhancing patient safety  with that i would like to acknowledge my  co-workers listed here  and also the funding source u.s food and  drug administration  and thank you all for your attention
 

